# VlogOps — line endings are LOAD-BEARING here, not a style preference.
#
# This repository has `core.autocrlf=true` and no root `.gitattributes`, so without this file a
# checkout on Windows and a checkout on Linux hold different bytes for the same committed file.
# For most files that is merely untidy. For two of them it changes a stored identity:
#
#   src/scribe/contract/*.md   the Scribe contract's sha256 IS its version. Two identities for
#                              one contract, decided by the checking-out operating system, would
#                              make `contract_id` and every `package_id` derived from it depend
#                              on where the draft happened to run.
#
#   db/*.sql, src/**, test/**  the proofs read and hash these; a CRLF surprise is exactly how a
#                              source-scanning control in this estate has silently broken before.
#
# `src/scribe/contract.mjs` folds CRLF before hashing anyway, and that is the mechanism. THIS
# FILE IS DEFENCE IN DEPTH — a checkout setting can be lost, and the identity must hold regardless.
# Neither one is permitted to be the only protection.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
